course: dictionary
lesson: 12201
title: Conformity: fitting in and following rules
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Conformity means behaving the same way as most other people, or following a rule or standard exactly. The clues are often in the words around it, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: «The school had a strong pressure towards conformity, so almost everyone wore the same coloured jumper.» The clues are pressure and almost everyone wore the same, so conformity means doing what the group does.
explain: The word can also mean following a rule. «The toy was tested and found to be in conformity with the safety rules.» Here it is not about copying friends. It means the toy meets the rules. Swap in your meaning to check: does «meets the safety rules» make sense? It does.
fact: Conformity means behaving the same way as most other people, or the way the rules expect.
fact: Conformity can also mean being in agreement with a rule, law or standard, as in «in conformity with the safety rules».
fact: «Pressure to conform» means feeling pushed to act like everyone else.
fact: You can think for yourself and still keep good rules, because the two are not the same thing.
fact: Products must be «in conformity with» safety standards, and marks such as the CE or UKCA mark show this.
exercise: «Everyone in the class wore the same trainers, and Sam bought a pair too, just to fit in.» What does this show? | Being different on purpose | Winning a race | Feeling cold | *Conformity: doing what most people do
exercise: What does «in conformity with the safety rules» mean? | Making up new rules | Breaking the safety rules | Forgetting the rules | *Following the safety rules
exercise: Which phrase means feeling pushed to act like everyone else? | Pressure to shout | Pressure to be late | Pressure to swim | *Pressure to conform
test: «The group showed social conformity: everyone repeated the same answer.» What is social conformity? | Arguing with everyone | Choosing a new hobby | Running very fast | *Acting like the group to fit in
test: Which sentence uses conformity to mean following a standard? | «The bottle was blue and shiny.» | «The bottle fell off the table.» | *«The bottle is in conformity with the safety standard.» | «The bottle was empty by lunch.»
exam: Why do companies check that a product is in conformity with safety standards? | *To make sure it is safe to use, because it meets the rules | To make it heavier | To make it a different colour from the others | To show it meets the safety rules, so it is safe to use
